  "limitations": [
    "Qualification covers native x86_64 Linux static C/Rust fixtures, not the guest package or a production cutover.",
    "Foreign static compilation, guest VM execution, and performance acceptance remain unqualified.",
    "Static ELF linkage removes the interpreter and DT_NEEDED imports; glibc still embeds paths for optional runtime data, so its Nix reference is preserved and reported.",
